  "projectNotes": "# Hainbach's Spotykach Tapes\nA collection of 36 sounds that Hainbach gifted to the community.\n\nAvailable as a download pack of 36 files to use as you want, all we ask is that you respect Hainbach and do not resell these as your own.\n\n## About this pack\nThis pack is straight from the cutting room of the past three years of my explorations. For every video I make, I spend hours making sample packs for my https://patreon.com/hainbach, and this pack I curated for Spotykach is a selection from the thousands of sounds there. You will find strange resonances from ancient speakers, pumping nuclear research equipment, esoteric oscillations, acoustic loops, tape squeals, early digital glitter, whimsical melodies, dark drones and much here. Its meant to be a little treasure chest for you to explore and find inspiration in. Happy stumbling!\n\n**Hainbach, Berlin, 19.04.2026**\n\n## Usage Context\n**Free to use in your music, no reselling as part of sample pack or instrument.**\n\n## About these tapes\nThese files are also downloadable as a ready to copy onto the SD card zipped folder.\n\nSorted into 6 themed tapes, by community member jonwtr, you might want to sprinkle them around differently and add your own sounds;  tweak this project and save it locally and then build it onto your SD card.\n\nI've organized them according to some intuitive categories, and wrote some notes to spark some ideas.\nHave fun with these and a special thanks to Hainbach for sharing this with our community.  \n\n--\nIf you didn't catch the reference with these titles, I can but say: ***Snap!***",
